# logue SDK API reference (agent summary)

## Oscillator entry points

Include `userosc.h` and implement the `user_osc` hook table.

```c
// Required hooks for a custom oscillator (v1.1.0 naming)
void OSC_INIT(uint32_t platform, uint32_t api);
void OSC_CYCLE(const user_osc_param_t *params, int32_t *yn, uint32_t frames);
void OSC_NOTEON(const user_osc_param_t *params);
void OSC_NOTEOFF(const user_osc_param_t *params);
void OSC_PARAM(uint16_t index, uint16_t value);
```

Note: Some docs abbreviate note hooks as `OSC_NOTE_ON(note, velocity)`; the v1.1.0
headers pass `user_osc_param_t` on note on/off. Read `userosc.h` for your SDK tree.

## Effect entry points

| Effect type | Header        | Required hooks                          |
|-------------|---------------|-----------------------------------------|
| Modulation  | `usermodfx.h` | MODFX_INIT, MODFX_PROCESS, MODFX_PARAM    |
| Delay       | `userdelfx.h` | DELFX_INIT, DELFX_PROCESS, DELFX_PARAM  |
| Reverb      | `userrevfx.h` | REVFX_INIT, REVFX_PROCESS, REVFX_PARAM |

## Key runtime types

```c
// user_osc_param_t (from userosc.h)
typedef struct {
  int32_t  shape_lfo;   // LFO value applied to shape
  uint16_t pitch;       // high byte: note number, low byte: fine (0-255)
  uint16_t cutoff;      // 0x0000–0x1fff
  uint16_t resonance;   // 0x0000–0x1fff
  uint16_t reserved0[3];
} user_osc_param_t;
```

## DSP helpers provided by the SDK

- `dsp::SimpleLFO` — bipolar/unipolar sine LFO with phase offset.
- `q31_to_f32()` / `f32_to_q31()` — fixed-point conversion (`utils/fixed_math.h`).
- `fsel(a, b, cond)` — branchless select.
- `osc_w0(pitch)` — phase increment from MIDI pitch field.
- Fast sinf / cosf approximations (use with care).

## Manifest requirements

Every unit needs a `manifest.json` declaring (SDK v1.1.0 shape):

- `header.platform`, `header.module` (`osc`, `modfx`, `delfx`, `revfx`)
- `header.api`, `header.name`, `header.version`, `header.num_param`
- `header.params` — array of `[name, min, max, unit]` per knob

Set `platform` to `nutekt-digital`, `minilogue-xd`, or `prologue` at build time.
Agent docs may also list logical `targets` (see `docs/platform-matrix.md`).
